#use(std/code)

#section{Indented blocks}::

A trailing #code{:} on a call's line takes the following indented block as
the call's body. A #emph{bare} call alone on its line (#code{#name} or
#code{#name(args)}, nothing else) is sugar for that: the #code{:} may be
elided, so #code|{#foo}| over an indented block means exactly #code|{#foo:}|
over it — not the other way round. Indentation is #strong{tabs only}, exactly
one tab per nesting level.

#code(lang: "plain")
	before
	#emph
		first level
		#strong
			second level
		first again
	after

Live:

before
#emph
	first level
	#strong
		second level
	first again
after

Blank lines never close a block — only a non-blank line with fewer tabs does.
Inside a markup block body a blank line is a paragraph break:

#code(lang: "plain")
	#blockquote
		first para

		second para
	tail

Live:

#blockquote
	first para

	second para
tail

The explicit #code{:} is what lets a call that already has an inline body
(here the section title) still take an indented block — the bare-call sugar
does not apply once a #code|{{body}}| is present:

#code(lang: "plain")
	#section{A titled section}:
		Its content is the indented block below the colon.

Corner cases:

#list
	#item: A line starting with spaces at a structure position is a reader error; so is jumping more than one level deeper at once.
	#item: The bare-call sugar applies only with #emph{no} inline body. A call that already carries an inline #code|{{body}}| keeps its block only via an explicit #code{:}: #code|{#section{Title}}| over an indented block is an error, but #code|{#section{Title}:}| over it works — title plus block content. (#code|{#section{Title}::}| is the un-indented #emph{hanging} variant; see the hanging-blocks page.)
	#item: A trailing #code{:} introduces a block #emph{only} when a deeper line follows. #code|{#code{index.yamd}:}| with nothing indented below is not an empty body — the #code{:} stays literal text (sentence punctuation). With no inline body, #code|{#name:}| at end of line is still an empty rest-of-line body, and #code|{#name: text}| is still a rest-of-line body.
	#item: A #code{: text} rest-of-line body followed by a deeper line is an error, not a guessed block — the body is already taken, so the deeper line is an orphan indent.
	#item: Raw block bodies (e.g. #code{#code}) strip one leading tab per level and keep everything after verbatim, including leading spaces — see the code page.
